      "Source.remaining continues to expose Buffer lexical text. Coalescing boundaries, 64 KiB cap, converted-window line fallback, pending CR/bracket deferral and malformed-prefix scans all use that lexical text, so converted ASCII newline or delimiter aliases cannot become physical scanner boundaries.",
      "character_data receives an exact source substring while Source storage and metadata are still live. When aliases exist it reconstructs the corresponding Slice and source_text normalizes only physical raw line endings. Ordinary plain text retains its earlier fast path and internal replacement text retains literal character-reference CR.",
      "Markup token Buffer.append retains conversion offsets before the fallible parsing closure. Comment/PI restoration and start/end-name identity checks finish before swap_decoded. No event retains a lexical view into the token.",
      "swap_decoded remains immediately after the parsing closure and before parsed? or source consumption: errors still publish current raw text, successful queued payloads remain owned, and metadata is discarded only after all lexical projections have finished. The existing fallible alias decode precedes owner mutation.",
      "Checked FFI input-context copy operates on original feed bytes independently of lexical projections; coalesced position byte counts still derive from Source raw widths."
    ],
